WEBVTT

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:05.489
Somatosensory or somatic tinnitus
is a term that reflects that for some

00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:09.630
individuals their experience
of tinnitus may change temporarily.

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:13.286
This may occur when they experience
different kinds of stimuli,

00:00:13.326 --> 00:00:16.269
such as muscle contractions
of the head and neck,

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:20.683
specific kinds of eye movements,
pressure on myofascial trigger points,

00:00:20.723 --> 00:00:26.430
stimulating regions of the hand or face,
or specific kinds of facial movements.

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:31.204
You may have seen videos on the internet
that teach these approaches and claim

00:00:31.244 --> 00:00:36.418
them as a cure for tinnitus, but research
suggests that these techniques are more

00:00:36.458 --> 00:00:42.390
likely to temporarily help those who experienced head or neck injuries and tinnitus.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:48.767
Please be cautious in your exploration
of alternative treatment methods,

00:00:48.807 --> 00:00:53.490
including acupuncture, hypnosis,
vitamins and herbs, and homeopathy.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:56.444
Many treatments are offered
on the internet and some

00:00:56.484 --> 00:00:59.270
of them claim to provide
a cure for tinnitus.

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:02.997
Knowing the biological aspects
of tinnitus that it is typically

00:01:03.037 --> 00:01:06.710
a sign of neural damage can
help protect you from scams.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:11.774
A cure may be found in the next few decades,
but until science reaches that point,

00:01:11.814 --> 00:01:15.696
you should be cautious about paying
money for tinnitus treatments.

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:17.610
There are many clinical trials in the U.S.

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:21.110
and elsewhere that are studying
possible treatments for tinnitus.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:25.310
Please research them
on clinicaltrials.gov.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:29.281
Legitimate clinical trials
typically do not charge any fee

00:01:29.321 --> 00:01:34.510
for participation and actually may
offer some reimbursement for your time.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:38.166
The pharmacological drugs
for tinnitus typically

00:01:38.206 --> 00:01:41.770
are not provided to treat
tinnitus symptoms themselves.

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:46.144
Instead, they are given to treat
problems such as insomnia and other sleep

00:01:46.184 --> 00:01:50.850
problems and reactions to having tinnitus,
such as depression and anxiety.

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:54.750
Please see the website link
listed on the PowerPoint slide.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:58.706
That link will connect you to a published
scientific analysis on the range

00:01:58.746 --> 00:02:03.150
of treatments for tinnitus,
including the use of pharmacological drugs.

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:07.278
The document by Maldonado
Fernandez, Shin, Scherer,

00:02:07.318 --> 00:02:11.010
and Murdin is listed
in the reference file.

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:15.910
Now we will discuss things you
can do for tinnitus symptoms.

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:19.810
The following slides are about
the audiological strategies for tinnitus.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:23.773
A person's sound environment refers
to the sounds in the external

00:02:23.813 --> 00:02:27.750
environment that you
are experiencing at any given moment.

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:32.511
One of the most important pieces
of advice for individuals with tinnitus

00:02:32.551 --> 00:02:38.290
is that you should make sure
that your sound environment is not silent.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:44.910
You should not have a quiet external
sound environment when you have tinnitus.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:48.550
This is because our brains crave stimuli.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:52.464
When there is no noise
in your external sound environment,

00:02:52.504 --> 00:02:58.590
your brain will more likely become more
aware of your internal tinnitus symptoms.

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:03.771
Hence, the number one piece of advice
is to make sure the room or environment

00:03:03.811 --> 00:03:08.110
you are in is not silent,
such as when you are trying to sleep.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:12.956
This can be done by adding different kinds
of sounds to one's sound environment.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:17.530
It is your choice what kind of sound
to add to your external environment.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:22.130
That will be based on your preferences
about the type of sound you want to hear.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.970
Your preferences can
change throughout the day.

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:28.622
Feel free to experiment with different
kinds of sounds for the purposes

00:03:28.662 --> 00:03:32.550
of adding to your sound environment
and managing your tinnitus.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:37.390
How do you add external sound
to your sound environment?

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:40.985
You can use mp3 players,
radios, sound machines,

00:03:41.025 --> 00:03:45.970
tabletop water fountains, fans,
and other items that make noise.

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:49.585
You can use sounds that are soothing,
such as classical music,

00:03:49.625 --> 00:03:52.870
new age music, nature sounds,
or meditation music.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:54.850
Any kind of music would work.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:58.012
Of course, you have to consider
the kind of music that works

00:03:58.052 --> 00:04:02.990
for your particular situation,
such as if you're trying to get to sleep.

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:06.847
Depending on your situation,
you can use sounds that engage your mind,

00:04:06.887 --> 00:04:11.670
like talk radio, the television,
or audio versions of your favorite books.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:16.610
It is your choice how you integrate
sound into your sound environment.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:19.955
Try experimenting with different
kinds of sounds to determine

00:04:19.995 --> 00:04:23.450
what works best for you
in a variety of situations.

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:29.123
It is advisable that everyone who has
tinnitus and who is going through this

00:04:29.163 --> 00:04:34.130
course to get checked by a physician
see reasons to do so in section one.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:38.590
Also consider a check
by an audiologist for hearing loss.

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:43.789
If you have hearing loss, hearing aids
enable individuals to better hear the sounds

00:04:43.829 --> 00:04:49.370
in their hearing environments, such
as soothing sounds or other background sounds.

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:53.191
Hearing aids bring in more
audiological stimuli to the brain,

00:04:53.231 --> 00:04:57.930
which may result in the brain
paying less attention to tinnitus.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:01.714
There are also hearing aids
on the market that can add sounds,

00:05:01.754 --> 00:05:05.870
like nature sounds or white noise,
to help manage tinnitus.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:10.897
While we encourage you to add sound
to your sound environment, keep in mind that,

00:05:10.937 --> 00:05:14.870
as previously mentioned, loud noise
can cause hearing loss and tinnitus,

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:18.969
or make your current levels of hearing
loss and tinnitus more severe.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:23.150
This means you should protect
yourself from loud sounds.

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:25.958
This includes the more obvious
causes of hearing issues,

00:05:25.998 --> 00:05:30.407
such as shooting guns at a range or while
hunting, but also less obvious causes,

00:05:30.447 --> 00:05:34.970
such as using power tools like weed
whackers, lawnmowers, and chainsaws.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:40.071
Further, very loud music in the car
at a concert or listening to loud music

00:05:40.111 --> 00:05:45.690
while wearing earphones can cause
audiological damage, hearing loss or tinnitus.

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:48.870
Traffic noise may also cause damage.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:53.461
Please try to be aware of the noise
level in your sound environment and take

00:05:53.501 --> 00:05:58.510
steps to modify it by wearing ear protection,
such as earplugs and earmuffs.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:04.106
In summary, adding sounds will
shift your brain's attention

00:06:04.146 --> 00:06:06.898
away from the internally
generated tinnitus noises

00:06:06.938 --> 00:06:11.520
to the external sound that you
choose in your sound environment.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:15.111
Because our brains crave stimuli,
your brain will notice

00:06:15.151 --> 00:06:19.710
tinnitus symptoms more when you
are in a very quiet environment.

00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:23.790
If you have hearing loss,
consider hearing aids.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:27.199
With more external audiological
stimuli available to you because

00:06:27.239 --> 00:06:31.390
of the hearing aids, your brain
may pay less attention to tinnitus.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.252
In summary, the most
important audiological

00:06:34.292 --> 00:06:37.590
tip is to add sound
to your sound environment.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:41.910
It is your choice about
the type of sound that you use.

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:45.062
Experiment with different types
of sounds for different situations,

00:06:45.102 --> 00:06:49.690
and you may find that it helps you
pay less attention to your tinnitus.

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:54.309
The next sections will deal
with understanding stress and choosing

00:06:54.349 --> 00:06:58.770
coping strategies according to the type
of stress that you are facing.

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:02.615
While this course is about tinnitus
and the stress that it can cause, the

00:07:02.655 --> 00:07:07.770
information about coping strategies may be
useful to you in many areas of your life.
